# Composer installs a release from GitHub's archive of the tag, and the archive holds only what this
# allow-list keeps: the PHP half - its code (backend/src), its migration files (backend/migrations), its
# resources (backend/resources) and the stand-in IAM a site's tests start (backend/testing, which answers nothing
# but under PHP's built-in server) - with composer.json, README.md and CHANGELOG.md. Everything else stays
# out, a folder added later too: the Angular workspace, the library's own tests, the workflows. Every
# site's build uploads vendor/ whole. CI builds the archive and checks the list
# (.github/scripts/check-archive.sh).
/* export-ignore
/backend !export-ignore
/backend/tests export-ignore
/composer.json !export-ignore
/README.md !export-ignore
/CHANGELOG.md !export-ignore

# What a release ships to be read byte for byte has LF line endings in every checkout and archive: a
# migration's last line is read (Japanese Academy's draft rule), and a test holds the SQL to the words.
/backend/migrations/** text eol=lf
/backend/resources/** text eol=lf

# A shell script with CRLF line endings does not run.
/.github/scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
